      ['skep pr open REPO --branch NAME [--base BRANCH] [--title TITLE]', 'Open a pull request for an existing local branch.'],
      ['skep pr merge REPO NUMBER [--method merge|squash|rebase]', 'Merge an open pull request. This is the one command that moves the base branch.'],
      ['skep pr close REPO NUMBER [--delete-branch]', 'Close a pull request without merging.'],
      ['skep repo list', 'Every repository skep can reach.'],
      ['skep repo refresh REPO', 'Fetch origin and fast-forward the default branch.'],
      ['skep repo push-baseline REPO [--base BRANCH]', 'Create the missing default branch on an empty origin.'],
    ],
    note: 'A worker can never push, pull, fetch or switch branches. skep itself pushes only when you ask: with <code>--pr</code> on an approval, <code>skep pr open</code> or <code>skep branch push</code>.',
  },
  {
    id: 'policy',
    eyebrow: 'Projects, policy and roles',
    title: 'Say what is allowed',
    lead: 'A project binds a repository to its policy. The policy commands read the rules, answer for one action, and lock the baseline.',
    rows: [
      ['skep project preview REPO [--pack PACK] [--strategy STRATEGY] [--phase PHASE] [--engine ENGINE] [--verify-command CMD]', 'Show what a setup would save, and save nothing.'],
      ['skep project setup REPO [--pack PACK] [--strategy STRATEGY] [--phase PHASE] [--engine ENGINE] [--verify-command CMD] [--group NAME] [--loopback-port PORT] [--codex-chatgpt-login | --no-codex-chatgpt-login] [--unlocked | --no-unlocked]', 'Save a project. It infers the verify command from the repository\'s own entry point; <code>--verify-command</code> pins one. A repository that is not a project yet needs <code>--pack</code> or <code>--strategy</code>. Also takes <code>--project-id</code>, <code>--name</code>, <code>--no-seed-schedules</code> and <code>--no-seed-commands</code>.'],
      ['skep project list', 'Every project.'],
      ['skep project show [PROJECT_ID] [--effective REPO]', 'One project\'s policy, or what a run against a repository would actually get.'],
      ['skep project set-phase PROJECT_ID PHASE', 'Move a project between phases (bootstrap, build, maintain).'],
      ['skep project remove PROJECT_ID', 'Unregister a project. skep forgets it; the folder is untouched.'],
      ['skep policy registry', 'Every policy setting skep has.'],
      ['skep policy rsop REPO', 'The resultant policy for a repository: each key, the layer that decided it, what it overrode.'],
      ['skep policy why REPO SCOPE ACTION VALUE [--role NAME] [--delegated-by ACTOR@ROLE]', 'Would this one action be allowed here, and which rule decides? Nothing is dispatched or recorded.'],
      ['skep policy explain SUBJECT', 'A template, <code>baseline</code> or <code>role:&lt;name&gt;</code> as an allow / ask / deny table.'],
      ['skep policy approve [--template NAME | --file PATH] [--reapprove] [--yes] [--diff]', 'Lock a template or a layer file as the policy baseline. <code>--diff</code> first replays recent decisions under the new layer and shows what flips.'],
      ['skep policy baseline [status|diff]', 'The approved baseline. <code>status</code> exits 1 when the file no longer matches its lock.'],
      ['skep policy migrate --dry-run', 'Replay the decision log under today\'s policy and list every verdict that changes. Writes nothing.'],
      ['skep policy decide SCOPE ACTION VALUE [--repo REPO] [--actor NAME] [--role NAME] [--delegated-by ACTOR@ROLE] [--read-only]', 'Decide one action for an agent outside skep, and record the decision.'],
      ['skep policy hook [--actor NAME]', 'The same decision as a Claude Code PreToolUse hook: payload on standard input, verdict as hook JSON.'],
      ['skep policy grants', 'Every learned grant: its id, what it matches, its lifetime, what it is bound to.'],
      ['skep policy revoke RULE_ID', 'Remove one learned grant. What it allowed asks again.'],
      ['skep policy decisions [--actor GLOB] [--since TIME] [--limit N] [--team ID]', 'The decision log, newest first, with counts per verdict.'],
      ['skep role list', 'Every role; <code>*</code> marks the one new chats open in.'],
      ['skep role show NAME', 'One role\'s record and its policy layer as a table.'],
      ['skep role use NAME [--chat ID]', 'Set the role new chats open in, or switch one chat.'],
      ['skep trust CHAT_ID [--bit private|untrusted]', 'Trust a chat again by clearing its taint bits. The chat deck\'s <code>/trust</code> is the same action.'],
    ],
  },
  {
    id: 'serve',
    eyebrow: 'The daemon and the chat',
    title: 'Talk to the assistant',
    lead: 'skep serve is the local daemon: the HTTP API, the web interface, the chat and the schedule ticker. skep chat is the same chat in a terminal.',
    rows: [
      ['skep serve [--host HOST] [--port PORT] [--worker-cmd COMMAND] [--no-readopt]', 'Run the daemon. It prints its address and an access token at startup. Workers still running from a previous serve are picked up again unless <code>--no-readopt</code>.'],
      ['skep chat [--url URL] [--chat ID] [--continue] [--thinking] [--role ROLE] [--oneshot MESSAGE] [--yes]', 'Talk to the assistant in the terminal. It needs a running <code>skep serve</code>.'],
      ['skep start [--host HOST] [--port PORT]', 'The older status dashboard. <code>skep serve</code> is the full daemon and is what you normally want.'],
      ['skep channel status', 'One line for each messenger channel: configuration, secret present or not, last delivery.'],
    ],
    options: {
      caption: 'Options of skep chat',
      rows: [
        ['--continue, --chat ID', 'Resume the most recent chat, or one by id.'],
        ['--role ROLE', 'Open the new chat in this role. The default is the one <code>skep role list</code> marks with <code>*</code>.'],
        ['--oneshot MESSAGE', 'Send one message to a new chat, print the reply as it streams, and exit. No prompts: cards the turn proposes are skipped and reported by id.'],
        ['--yes', 'With <code>--oneshot</code>: confirm every card this turn proposes, once. Never a policy card; those stay pending.'],
        ['--thinking', 'Show the model\'s thinking, dimmed.'],
        ['--url URL', 'The daemon\'s address. Default: <code>$SKEP_SERVE_URL</code>, else the port this home\'s serve recorded, else port 8765 on this machine.'],
      ],
    },
  },
  {
    id: 'schedule',
    eyebrow: 'Repeat and reuse',
    title: 'Schedules, templates, skills and memory',
    lead: 'Recurring runs, saved task shapes, and the two things skep can learn only with your approval.',
    rows: [
      ['skep schedule add NAME REPO [INSTRUCTIONS] --every 1d [--template NAME] [--param KEY=VALUE] [--caste CASTE] [--ref REF] [--network DOMAIN] [--env-allow ENV] [--role NAME] [--start-at TIME] [--once]', 'Add a recurring run, from instructions or a saved template. <code>--every</code> takes 30s, 5m, 2h or 1d. <code>--start-at</code> sets the first run (a time with no zone is UTC); <code>--once</code> fires once, then disables.'],
      ['skep schedule list', 'Every schedule.'],
      ['skep schedule remove NAME', 'Remove a schedule.'],
      ['skep schedule health', 'How each schedule has been doing.'],
      ['skep tick [--worker-cmd COMMAND]', 'Dispatch every due schedule once, for cron. A running <code>skep serve</code> does this itself.'],
      ['skep template add [NAME] [--instructions TEXT] [--from FILE] [options]', 'Author a workflow template, from flags or a .toml or .json file.'],
      ['skep template list', 'Every template.'],
      ['skep template show NAME', 'One template in full.'],
      ['skep template suggest NAME REPO INSTRUCTIONS [--save]', 'Suggest a template from remembered approvals; <code>--save</code> keeps it.'],
      ['skep template remove NAME', 'Remove a template. <code>skep template delete</code> is the same command.'],
      ['skep template rename OLD_NAME NEW_NAME', 'Rename a template; schedules bound to it follow.'],
      ['skep skill …', 'The learned-skill lifecycle: propose, list, show, test, approve, reject, export, seed, shelf, promote, packs, import-md, import. Nothing is admitted without your approval.'],
      ['skep skill shelf [list|add|remove] [PATH]', 'Register a directory of Agent Skills, for example <code>~/.claude/skills</code>.'],
      ['skep memory …', 'Durable memory, gated by proposals: list, search, show, forget, add (the operator records a fact directly, with no proposal), proposals, propose, approve, reject, approve-batch, reject-batch.'],
    ],
  },
  {
    id: 'govern',
    eyebrow: 'Agents you run elsewhere',
    title: 'Govern an agent skep did not start',
    lead: 'Two ways to put skep\'s policy in front of an agent running in another tool. Both decide from the same policy and record the decision; neither is a sandbox.',
    rows: [
      ['skep acp govern [--repo PATH] [--actor NAME] -- AGENT_ARGV…', 'The process an ACP client starts in place of the agent. It answers the agent\'s permission requests from policy and records them.'],
      ['skep acp doctor -- AGENT_ARGV…', 'Start the agent, open a dry session and print what skep can govern in it. Sends no prompt.'],
      ['skep acp install-hint', 'Print the rows to paste into T3 Code\'s Local ACP command dialog.'],
      ['skep policy hook', 'The Claude Code PreToolUse hook (listed above with the policy commands).'],
    ],
    note: 'What each one covers and does not cover is on <a class="c-green" href="/agents.html#hook">the agents page</a>.',
  },
  {
    id: 'ops',
    eyebrow: 'Ops and imports',
    title: 'Nodes, ops checks and imports',
    lead: 'A smaller surface: governed operations checks against registered machines, and a one-way import from Hermes.',
    rows: [
      ['skep node add NODE_ID [--name NAME] [--host HOST] [--kind local|ssh|container] [--trust LEVEL] [--cap CAP]', 'Register a node and the ops capabilities it allows.'],
      ['skep node list', 'Registered nodes.'],
      ['skep ops run CHECK --node NODE [--approve] [--arg KEY=VALUE]', 'Resolve an ops check against a node. Without <code>--approve</code> it is a dry-run plan.'],
      ['skep ops schedule add …', 'Add a conservative ops schedule.'],
      ['skep hermes import [--hermes-home PATH] [--dry-run]', 'Stage Hermes memory, skills and sessions behind skep\'s existing gates: they arrive as proposals and drafts.'],
    ],
  },
];

---

<Base
  title="CLI"
  description="Every skep command, grouped by what you are trying to do: set up, run a task, review and land, policy, the daemon and chat, schedules, and the chat's slash commands."
  active="cli"
>
  <Section eyebrow="CLI" lead="Every top-level command, grouped by what you are trying to do. For the exact parser output, add --help to any command.">
    <h1 slot="heading" class="t-h2">CLI reference</h1>
    <div class="grid grid-2" style="align-items: start">
      <div class="grid">
        <CodeBlock code="skep [--home HOME] [--version] <command>" lang="text" title="shape of a command" copy={false} />
        <div class="prose">
          <ul>
            <li><code>--home HOME</code> selects the state directory. It goes before the command. Default: <code>$SKEP_HOME</code>, else <code>~/.skep</code>.</li>
            <li><code>--version</code> prints the package version and the worker contract version.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
      <Terminal code={versionOut} title="skep --version" captured="skep --version; the two numbers are filled in from this release's sources" />
    </div>
    <nav class="row jump" aria-label="Sections of this page">
      {groups.map((group) => <a class="link-arrow" href={`#${group.id}`}>{group.eyebrow}</a>)}
      <a class="link-arrow" href="#deck">Slash commands</a>
    </nav>
  </Section>

  {
    groups.map((group, index) => (
      <Section id={group.id} band={index % 2 === 0} eyebrow={group.eyebrow} title={group.title} lead={group.lead}>
        <div class="grid">
          <Table caption={`Commands: ${group.eyebrow.toLowerCase()}`}>
            <thead>
              <tr><th scope="col">Command</th><th scope="col">What it does</th></tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              {group.rows.map(([command, what]) => (
                <tr>
                  <th scope="row" class="cmd"><code>{command.split(' ').map((token) => (<><span class="tok">{token}</span>{' '}</>))}</code></th>
                  <td set:html={what} />
                </tr>
              ))}
            </tbody>
          </Table>
          {group.id === 'run' && (
            <div class="grid grid-2" style="align-items: start">
              <CodeBlock
                code={`$ skep run /path/to/repo "fix the failing test" --execution-mode sandbox\n$ skep run /path/to/repo "fix the failing test" --engine codex --execution-mode sandbox`}
                title="examples"
              />
              <Callout kind="limit" title="Choose the mode on every run">
                <p>
                  Only <code>--execution-mode sandbox</code> puts the worker behind the OS sandbox.
                  A run with no model configured fails: skep's own worker then falls back to a fixed
                  routine that handles one Python hello-world task.
                </p>
              </Callout>
            </div>
          )}
          {group.options && (
            <Table caption={group.options.caption}>
              <thead>
                <tr><th scope="col">Option</th><th scope="col">What it does</th></tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                {group.options.rows.map(([option, what]) => (
                  <tr>
                    <th scope="row" class="cmd"><code>{option.split(' ').map((token) => (<><span class="tok">{token}</span>{' '}</>))}</code></th>
                    <td set:html={what} />
                  </tr>
                ))}
              </tbody>
            </Table>
          )}
          {group.note && <p class="prose-width t-small c-mut" set:html={group.note} />}
        </div>
      </Section>
    ))
  }

  <Section id="deck" band={groups.length % 2 === 0} eyebrow="Slash commands" title="The command deck" lead="In the web chat and in skep chat, a message that starts with / is a command of yours. The model never sees it.">
    <div class="grid">
      <Table caption="The deck, read at build from the web app's COMMANDS table">
        <thead>
          <tr><th scope="col">Command</th><th scope="col">What it does</th><th scope="col">Effect</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {deck.map((row) => (
            <tr>
              <th scope="row" class="cmd"><code>{row.usage.split(' ').map((token) => (<><span class="tok">{token}</span>{' '}</>))}</code></th>
              <td>{row.desc}</td>
              <td><Chip kind={row.effect.kind}>{row.effect.label}</Chip></td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </Table>
      <div class="grid grid-2" style="align-items: start">
        <div class="prose">
          <ul>
            <li>A command marked <strong>confirm card</strong> changes something, so it shows a card and waits for your yes.</li>
            <li><code>/trust</code> and <code>/steer</code> act at once, with no card. In the terminal, a typed <code>/approve</code> or <code>/deny</code> is the decision itself and is not asked twice.</li>
            <li><code>/approve</code> and <code>/deny</code> take a review id or a card id. <code>/land</code> takes a task id. Approving a completed run's review already applies its patch; <code>/land</code> lands a completed run directly.</li>
            <li><code>/workon</code> is not a selector: it makes a directory a workspace, with a git baseline and a project.</li>
            <li>There is no command that starts a run. Ask for the work in a plain message and confirm the card the assistant proposes, or use <code>skep run</code>.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <Table caption="Terminal only: these five exist in skep chat, not in the web chat">
          <thead>
            <tr><th scope="col">Command</th><th scope="col">What it does</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {terminalOnly.map(([usage, what]) => (
              <tr>
                <th scope="row" class="cmd"><code>{usage.split(' ').map((token) => (<><span class="tok">{token}</span>{' '}</>))}</code></th>
                <td>{what}</td>
              </tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </Table>
      </div>
      <p class="prose-width t-small c-mut">
        The same reference as one markdown file, with more detail on roles and delegation:
        <a class="c-green" href="/docs/cli-reference.html">CLI reference doc</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>
</Base>

